WEBVTT

00:00:00.035 --> 00:00:03.762
An owner can say, "I want this to feel like a tidy inbox,"

00:00:04.087 --> 00:00:06.908
while also saying they do not want a copy of their email.

00:00:07.605 --> 00:00:10.646
The phrase conveys the experience but not the full feature

00:00:10.681 --> 00:00:11.088
list.

00:00:11.529 --> 00:00:14.385
Ask the agent to translate the metaphor into observable

00:00:14.420 --> 00:00:17.218
behavior and identify choices that remain.

00:00:17.601 --> 00:00:19.807
The owner decides what the metaphor means.

00:00:20.132 --> 00:00:22.721
This is particularly useful when an idea contains

00:00:22.779 --> 00:00:26.808
examples, comparisons, or partial solutions that could

00:00:26.843 --> 00:00:28.549
otherwise become hidden requirements.
